guide-title = How to get your export from Snapchat
guide-intro = If you haven't downloaded your Memories yet, request them from Snapchat first. It takes four steps.
guide-step-number = Step { $n }
guide-step1-title = Open My Data
guide-step1-body = In a web browser, go to <b>accounts.snapchat.com</b>, sign in and choose <b>My Data</b>.
guide-step2-title = Choose Memories and JSON files
guide-step2-body = Tick <b>Export your Memories</b> and <b>Export JSON Files</b>. The JSON files hold the dates and places.
guide-step3-title = Choose All Time
guide-step3-body = Set the date range to <b>All Time</b>, then submit the request.
guide-step4-title = Download every part
guide-step4-body = Snapchat emails you when the export is ready, which can take <b>up to 7 days</b>. Download every ZIP file it offers as soon as you can.

notes-title = Before you request it
note-expiry-title = Download links expire quickly
note-expiry-body = The download links may stop working after about 3 days. Download all parts soon after the email arrives. If they expire, request a new export.
note-meo-title = My Eyes Only is not included
note-meo-body = Memories in My Eyes Only are left out of the export, and { -product } can't recover them. Move the ones you want out of My Eyes Only in Snapchat before you request the export.
note-2027-title = What changes in January 2027
note-2027-body = From January 2027, Snapchat archives Memories that are more than a year old and fall outside your oldest 5 GB. Archived Memories stay stored on Snapchat and show as thumbnails; opening, editing or sharing them needs a paid storage plan. Snap says it won't delete Memories because you don't upgrade.
